<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="025" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author ArchTest guarding no cleartext secret patterns in Cosmos ProvisioningRun rows</title>
    <phase>C Wave C1 — Registry Schema + Cosmos Model</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Test-modifying task per root CLAUDE.md §8 override — any task touching tests/** triggers unconditional FULL rigor (code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5). Enforces §4D-adjacent tenant-isolation invariant with CATASTROPHIC severity — the ArchTest prevents cleartext-secret leakage to Cosmos rows.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Standard ArchTest authoring following the existing GodClassGuardTests / ADR-013 injection-guard pattern; canonical exemplar is available in tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/**. spec.md §Assumptions "Sonnet 5 @ high for Dataverse solution + Cosmos schema" (this is the paired invariant enforcer).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Deps on task 024 — needs the RunParameters / KeyVaultSecretRef types the test asserts against.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>024</deps>
    <tags>testing, integration-test, azure, l2-controlplane</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Author an ArchTest in tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/** that regex-scans (a) all Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane types with a Cosmos-persisted attribute or namespace ancestry for a string-typed Secrets/Password/Key/ClientSecret property, AND (b) any test fixture/sample data payload targeting the runs container for known secret-shaped patterns (KV RBAC keys, connection strings, sk_/pat_/token_ prefixes) NOT wrapped in @Microsoft.KeyVault(...). The test MUST fail on hit; must pass on the RunParameters + KeyVaultSecretRef shape authored in task 024.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with ArchTest / NetArchTest / Roslyn source-analysis expertise. Follow ADR-038 KEEP-path testing discipline; test asserts a structural invariant, not runtime behavior.</role>
  <goal>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CosmosProvisioningSecretGuardTests.cs (or equivalent) exists and (a) fails on any Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane type that exposes a string-typed secret-shaped property (Secret/Password/Key/ClientSecret) intended for Cosmos persistence, (b) fails on any test-fixture literal matching known secret prefixes not wrapped in KV URI reference syntax, (c) passes on the task-024 KeyVaultSecretRef pattern. The test is sequenced into the r3 forcing-functions ecosystem via CI-wiring coordinated PR (Phase H).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-27 acceptance: "no cleartext secret string matches any known secret pattern in Cosmos rows." Design.md §4D I3-adjacent + §6.2 secret-storage discipline require KV URI reference only. Historically Spaarke has already caught 3 AI-Search-key aliases + 6 orphan template references from lack of a mechanical guard (§7.9 rename map). Without this ArchTest, any future PR could add a string Password/Secret property to a Cosmos-persisted POCO with no CI signal. Severity: CATASTROPHIC (secret leak to a queryable audit-log store).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CosmosProvisioningSecretGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/GodClassGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Models/RunParameters.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Models/KeyVaultSecretRef.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="024" status="pending">RunParameters + KeyVaultSecretRef POCO types define the compliant shape the test's happy-path asserts.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: this ArchTest is a KEEP-path test (structural invariant); coverage is observation not gate. Do NOT mock HttpMessageHandler; do NOT test runtime behavior.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the test enforces ADR-028 secret-storage rule for Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane types only; do NOT expand scope to unrelated BFF services (those have their own guards — bff-extensions.md §F.1 anti-pattern rule).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (this task only): author the ArchTest + a passing sample + a documented failing sample in a comment; do NOT edit .github/workflows/** (that is Phase H coordinated PR per root CLAUDE.md §10 ci-workflows=Y).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST use regex patterns covering known secret prefixes: sk_, pat_, ghp_, xoxb-, xoxp-, connection-string format (AccountKey=..., SharedAccessKey=..., Server=... Password=...), Azure primary/secondary key shape (44+ char base64), and any string property named /^(Secret|Password|Key|ClientSecret|ApiKey|ConnectionString)/i on a type in the Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane namespace.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST include a negative-case assertion: RunParameters.Secrets typed as IDictionary&lt;string, KeyVaultSecretRef&gt; MUST PASS the test (compliant shape).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ArchTest authoring; cleartext-secret-guard</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/god-class-ratchet.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="GodClassGuardTests (ArchTest exemplar)" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/GodClassGuardTests.cs">Mirror the assembly-scanning + type-filtering approach; use the same test-framework harness (xUnit + NetArchTest or Roslyn direct).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the RIGOR LEVEL declaration (FULL + reason — test-modifying override). Load spec.md FR-27, design.md §6.2 + §4D I3, ADR-028, ADR-038, GodClassGuardTests.cs exemplar.</step>
    <step order="1">Enumerate the regex patterns + property-name patterns to guard (as specified in the constraints section).</step>
    <step order="2">Author tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CosmosProvisioningSecretGuardTests.cs with two Facts: (a) Sprk_Provisioning_ControlPlane_types_have_no_string_secret_properties — scans all types under the L2 namespace for a string-typed property whose name matches secret-shape regex; (b) Test_fixtures_targeting_runs_container_have_no_cleartext_secret_literals — scans test-fixture JSON payloads under tests/**/fixtures/** referencing runs-container shape for secret-prefix literals NOT wrapped in @Microsoft.KeyVault(...).</step>
    <step order="3">Add a compliant-shape assertion: assert typeof(RunParameters).GetProperty("Secrets").PropertyType is IDictionary&lt;string, KeyVaultSecretRef&gt;.</step>
    <step order="4">Author a documented failing sample (as a commented-out type in the test file, or a temporary type behind a #if false block) so future readers see what a violation looks like.</step>
    <step order="5">Run dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ — verify both Facts pass against the task-024 shape.</step>
    <step order="6">Report the ArchTest to Phase H as a candidate for CI-workflow gating (per root CLAUDE.md §10 ci-workflows=Y coordinated-PR rule); do NOT touch .github/workflows/** yourself.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation (e.g. regex catalog additions, test-framework choice) in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the test framework (NetArchTest vs raw Roslyn) or the shape of RunParameters produced by task 024 differs from the design assumption above, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT weaken the assertion to force a pass.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The Spaarke.ArchTests suite exists (GodClassGuardTests, ADR-013 injection guards, layer-violation guards per spec.md § New Components row 12) — extending is the pattern. Grep of tests/Spaarke.ArchTests for "Cosmos" + "secret" returns none.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this joins the existing ArchTest suite as a new Fact class; test infrastructure (assembly-scanning + xUnit) reused.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this guard, a future PR could add a string ClientSecret property to any Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane POCO and land it silently; the row would then persist a cleartext secret to a Cosmos audit-log store queryable by anyone with Reader-role. Severity: CATASTROPHIC (matches §4D I2/I4/I5 severity per spec.md § New Components row 12). Concrete failure: task 024's KeyVaultSecretRef discipline degrades to string within one release without a mechanical enforcer.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CosmosProvisioningSecretGuardTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ project, dotnet test exits 0; both new Facts pass against the task-024 RunParameters + KeyVaultSecretRef shape.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a synthetic violating type (Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Fixtures.BadShape with public string ClientSecret {get;set;}), the first Fact FAILS with a clear diagnostic naming the type + property.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a synthetic test-fixture JSON containing "sk_live_..." NOT wrapped in @Microsoft.KeyVault, the second Fact FAILS with a clear diagnostic naming the fixture path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no changes to .github/workflows/** in this task (Phase H coordinated PR owns that per §10 ci-workflows=Y).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the test does NOT touch runtime code paths or mock any handler (ADR-038 compliance).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-27 acceptance + §4D I3-adjacent. Sequences into the r3 forcing-functions ecosystem (per plan.md Phase C Wave C6) via Phase H coordinated PR with ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1. Regex catalog is a living list — new secret prefixes discovered in the wild should be added here rather than in ad-hoc PR reviews.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
